 [17592186175957 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying the Point of Fastest Increase of a Logistic Growth Model" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175957 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186175803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175957 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "7293561d-2ddf-581d-b086-9754fdb2ff16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319233 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186321133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186480643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186480661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186480676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186516827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186516864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1039 "Determining the Carrying Capacity of a Logistic Growth Model In Context" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186175875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176020 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "4728b3c6-a600-569d-922e-228e9f6fb2a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176021 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048578 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176021 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176303 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176021 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176021 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176021 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176021 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253490 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176021 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176021 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186321127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176021 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186480644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176021 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186480660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176021 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186480677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176021 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186480697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176021 #edb/ref 1039 "Determining the Carrying Capacity of a Logistic Growth Model" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176021 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186175876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176021 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "91856ca3-4d9c-51c4-910b-27acba52156e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176102 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176684 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176102 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176102 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176102 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176102 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176102 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176102 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176102 #edb/ref 1045 "Qualitative Analysis of the Logistic Growth Equation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176102 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186176802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176102 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176102 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176102 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "ae699ea5-a992-5568-9ccc-711c674348a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176305 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186174088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176305 #edb/ref 1069 "q-118474" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176305 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176305 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following differential equation for the function $y=y(t):$\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=1\\,000y-10{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=40\n$$\n\nWhat is ${lim}_{t\\to \\infty }y(t)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176305 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cb420906-a342-521a-b8a1-6dfcb9eb4dbe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176305 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176305 #edb/ref 1074 "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nA diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](images/57/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's factor the right-hand side of the given equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=10y(100-y),\\,y(0)=40.\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=100.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $100.$\n\nFor a given logistic growth model, $y\\to a$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }y(t)=100.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176684 #edb/ref 1061 27108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176684 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d19c0f9f-80cc-5cf8-9f9a-1685e2ae53c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176684 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186175957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176797 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176797 #edb/ref 1061 35102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176797 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dd1fcac6-2708-5449-8133-f0e4daba018d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176797 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176020 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176798 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176798 #edb/ref 1061 35103 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176798 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0b510a99-00f3-5621-8ddb-4da0432e0388" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176798 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176799 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176799 #edb/ref 1061 35104 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176799 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2b3e0981-7dcf-5a80-b4a4-1a180100a2d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176799 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186177031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176802 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176802 #edb/ref 1061 35114 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176802 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ad747121-27b0-5c58-8372-2eae12c1e5f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176802 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186177033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176803 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176684 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176803 #edb/ref 1061 35116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176803 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ce23de13-efb4-50d3-a7f4-3e6500a63fbd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176803 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186177034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177031 #edb/ref 1064 "In general, the logistic growth boundary value problem for the function $y(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\ny' = ky(a-y), \\qquad y(0) = y_0,\n$$\n\nwhere $k > 0,$ and $0 < y < a.$\n\nA diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](images/00/00478583a9bc76980b898db4f846f323511026c1c6ac7b79e3f047575a015305.png)\n\nNote the following:\n\n- In practical situations, we usually set $t > 0.$ If we relax this constraint, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\lim_{t\\to-\\infty}{y(t)} = 0.\n$$\n\n \nThis behavior can be confirmed using an analysis similar to what we saw earlier.\n\n- The parameter $a$ is the **carrying capacity,** and is the limiting value of $y(t)$ for large $t.$ We can write\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\lim_{t\\to\\infty}{y(t)} = a.\n$$\n\n \nIf $y(t)$ represents how some population changes with time, the carrying capacity gives the maximum possible population.\n\n- We have assumed that $0 < y < a$ for all $t.$ Other cases are possible, though we do not consider those here." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177031 #edb/ref 1065 5714 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177031 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3f070df6-1d9d-5050-b509-d48d330c4709" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177031 #edb/ref 1067 "Some Key Features of a Logistic Growth Curve" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177033 #edb/ref 1064 "For some differential equations, it's possible to sketch the solution curves *without* calculating the general solution. Instead, we gather information about the solutions using the differential equation itself.\n\nAs an example, consider the following logistic growth equation: \n\n$$\ny' = 5y(10-y)\n$$\n\nIn practical applications, we're usually interested in the domain $t > 0,$ so we will stick to this constraint for the moment.\n\nThe equation is autonomous, so let's start by finding the equilibrium solutions. Setting up the equation $y'(t) = 0$ gives\n\n$$\n5y(10-y) = 0.\n$$\n\nSo, there are two equilibrium solutions, $y=0,$ and $y=10.$ Let's create a diagram and plot these two solutions.\n\n![](images/98/98d52420673e65eedf5679e57b9c562f8a8eeabde24d0d2ed4fff827a6447fc2.png)\n\nWe will now sketch a solution curve that lies between these two equilibrium solutions. \n\nNotice the following:\n\n- Since $0 < y < 10$ for all $t,$ we have that $5y(10-y)$ is positive for all $t.$\n\n- Therefore, $y'(t)$ is positive for all $t.$\n\n- Hence, $y(t)$ is increasing for all $t.$\n\nUsing this information, we can start to sketch a solution curve.\n\n![](images/ce/ce6f493f4c2830acf42e189ace04027f8452ec3df92d24b9d223f92848832996.png)\n\nNext, we note the following regarding the end-behavior of our solution:\n\n- The expression $5y(10-y)\\to 0$ as $y\\to10.$\n\n- Therefore, $y'\\to 0$ as $y\\to 10.$\n\nIn other words, the curve flattens as $y$ approaches $10.$ Adding this behavior to our diagram, we get a complete sketch of the solution curve.\n\n![](images/f3/f329f3cd49d61c3a1e2838397521cdd6d3bbefc7dadd09d1dd25b00767a0cd37.png)\n\nGathering information about the solutions to a differential equation without solving it is called **qualitative analysis.**" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177033 #edb/ref 1065 5718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177033 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "05ebc248-7295-5381-964a-30c7e3b638e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177033 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177034 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's go back to the following logistic growth equation:\n\n$$\ny' = 5y(10-y), \\qquad y(0) = y_0.\n$$\n\nThe logistic growth curve for this problem is sketched below.\n\n![](images/0a/0a225fd04f81bd65e1bad3ff14097563d112a16e3847aac26cc86591533ea5d0.png)\n\nThe curve contains an inflection point, that is, a point where $y(t)$ is growing at its fastest possible rate. What information can we deduce about this point? \n\nTo find the inflection point, we solve $y''(t) = 0.$ First, we differentiate the differential equation using implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″} & =(5y)^{′}\\cdot (10-y)+(5y)\\cdot (10-y)^{′} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (10-y)\\cdot {y}^{′}+(5y)\\cdot (-1)\\cdot {y}^{′} \\\\  & ={y}^{′}\\cdot (5\\cdot (10-y)+(5y)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & ={y}^{′}\\cdot (50-5y-5y) \\\\  & ={y}^{′}\\cdot (50-10y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to solve $y''(t) = 0,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\ny'\\cdot\\left(50-10y\\right) = 0.\n$$\n\nWe know that $y'$ is increasing for all $t,$ so $y'\\neq 0.$ Therefore, we must have\n\n$$\n50-10y = 0\\quad \\Rightarrow\\quad y = 5.\n$$\n\nLet's mark this on our diagram.\n\n![](images/75/75d0363483e1bda70decb171466fe9e506eb0da80d0e78ed893bb61551ae9d44.png)\n\nThe fact that the inflection point occurs when $y$ is precisely half the carrying capacity is *not* a coincidence. In fact, this is always the case. The general situation is shown below.\n\n![](images/77/7754f42adbb938c1d07ab2636a4c24f1cd0bc8536c974af2497e997589efa115.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177034 #edb/ref 1065 5719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177034 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "9032224d-2537-52e4-a688-8e341433ca18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177034 #edb/ref 1067 "Identifying the Point of Fastest Increase" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516109 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186516905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516109 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186516915 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516109 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186516918 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516109 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186516942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516109 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186516971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516109 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516109 #edb/ref 1045 "Qualitative Analysis of the Logistic Growth Equation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516109 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186516918 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516109 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516109 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516109 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "df4cdd91-8906-5e4a-b0e5-b2f695c09521" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516116 #edb/ref 1080 "600" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516116 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516116 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "02150670-428b-56e2-9985-6194ff4b8ee1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516136 #edb/ref 1080 "1\\,000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516136 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516136 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0c56636a-f906-5735-8c37-7b2138e8f77d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516140 #edb/ref 1080 "75\\,000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516140 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516140 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0cfd9676-eb74-5ebe-b031-0a788f78718e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516222 #edb/ref 1080 "1\\,3