ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516413 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8f83a6a6-3e56-5e96-b0ee-342a84b5b56d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516517 #edb/ref 1080 "320" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516517 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516517 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bf315d70-83f5-5ea5-abd9-3ae3cfc47fdb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516520 #edb/ref 1080 "1\\,000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516520 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516520 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c00bef54-cb61-5193-b9dc-726065db63fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516558 #edb/ref 1080 "130\\,000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516558 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516558 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d449452a-bba6-5329-88f3-21fa31072558" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516618 #edb/ref 1080 "45\\,000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516618 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516618 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f4473ebd-4861-56d2-8435-0aad1abb7b6e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516628 #edb/ref 1080 "860" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516628 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516628 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f7d2bf34-d828-5bcd-970b-c54ad54643d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516629 #edb/ref 1080 "13\\,000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516629 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516629 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f8137660-b678-5be7-9f4e-4e308f57cd8b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516702 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516702 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516136 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516702 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516702 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516702 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516702 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516702 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516702 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186516253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516702 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "701ad097-1360-59f4-8891-d19c7b1ca762" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516714 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516222 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516714 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516232 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516714 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516409 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516714 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516714 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516714 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516714 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516714 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186516558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516714 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "85a62696-1e6e-54dd-bb76-a23cc2767801" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516730 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516730 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516730 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516730 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186516239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516730 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "aa8b8268-0d26-5cf4-8d60-0789f0a8afa9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516740 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516140 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516740 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516233 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516740 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516740 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516740 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186516618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516740 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516740 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516740 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186516266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516740 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c19ec431-2d31-55ac-9370-03580e2d85ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516827 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516714 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516827 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119848" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516827 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516827 #edb/ref 1071 "The population $y(t)$ of elephants on a certain African wildlife reserve follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=26y-0.0002{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=120,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in years, since the observations began. According to this model, what is the maximum possible population of elephants?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516827 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "94d0a8c6-e1cc-589d-baf5-ae5d11bc5ecc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516827 #edb/ref 1074 "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe carrying capacity $a$ represents the maximum possible population. A diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](images/57/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =26y-0.0002{y}^{2} \\\\  & =0.0002y(130\\,000-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=130\\,000.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $130\\,000,$ and we conclude that the number of elephants cannot exceed $130\\,000.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516840 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516740 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516840 #edb/ref 1069 "q-15495" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516840 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516840 #edb/ref 1071 "A rumor is spreading in a city. The rate of growth in the number of people $P(t)$ who heard the rumor follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=12P-0.000\\,2{P}^{2},\\,P(0)=2\\,000.\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in hours. For which value of $P$ is the number of people who heard the rumor growing at the fastest possible rate?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516840 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b63e7390-032d-5732-93f4-683f3a627416" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516840 #edb/ref 1074 "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](images/9d/9d8f5340bba4d3c407e43f2bc64a4aa2ea986be89b8024baaa4e8ae65e96e5d5.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =12P-0.000\\,2{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.000\\,02P(60\\,000-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=60\\,000.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $60\\,000,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 60\\,000=30\\,000.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516842 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516730 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516842 #edb/ref 1069 "q-353486" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516842 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516842 #edb/ref 1071 "The population $P(t)$ of elk in a protected national park follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=5P-0.001{P}^{2},\\,P(0)=200,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in years. For which value of $P$ is the elk population growing at the fastest possible rate?\n\n$P=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516842 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b8a8e489-11e9-52ae-86cf-436bdb177f60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516842 #edb/ref 1074 "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](images/90/9019b26b417c757bbfab79afb39379c1fc7a892bc44e934c6f23c339deacfd68.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =5P-0.001{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.001P(5000-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=5000.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $5000,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5000=2500.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516864 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516702 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516864 #edb/ref 1069 "q-118558" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516864 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516864 #edb/ref 1071 "The population $y(t)$ of beavers in a river follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=0.2y(8-\\frac{y}{100}),\\,y(0)=200,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in years, since the observations began. According to this model, what is the maximum possible beaver population?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516864 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f4a129bc-20d0-5e0c-8e4d-26304c226b31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516864 #edb/ref 1074 "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity. \n\nThe carrying capacity $a$ represents the maximum possible population. A diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](images/57/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the right-hand side of the given equation so that it matches the form above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =0.2y(8-\\frac{y}{100}) \\\\  & =0.2y(\\frac{800-y}{100}) \\\\  & =\\frac{0.2y}{100}(800-y) \\\\  & =0.002y(800-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=800.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $800,$ and we conclude that the number of beavers cannot exceed $800.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516905 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186516915 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516905 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "547b9566-7a7e-5c10-8c3a-e62cae9ff92e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516905 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186516864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516915 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186516971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516915 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6b2c3692-cb7d-5953-88f2-5e6b531cfc44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516915 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186516827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516918 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186516942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516918 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6f1e6e85-1cc9-56f5-81c5-125a6a2d7028" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516918 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186516840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516942 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186516905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516942 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9fd0633c-ca54-5dbc-adf5-6d3546b046c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516942 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516971 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d4938297-4932-5247-bb96-9911519542a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516971 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186516842 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
